Imports:
  - Types:
      - Table
    From: lib/mergeset

Usages:
  god_package: |
    This is VictoriaMetrics's largest and most tightly-coupled package: ~14,100 non-test lines
    across 31 files (index_db.go alone is 3,482 lines, storage.go 2,687), with a test suite
    (~22,700 lines) larger than the production source of most other lib/ packages combined. Only
    22 top-level types are exported; the real complexity sits below the export boundary in
    unexported table/partition/indexDB layers that reach directly into each other's internals
    rather than through accessor abstractions (Storage -> table -> partitionWrapper.pt ->
    partition.idb -> indexDB, all raw field access). Both table and partition carry a field
    back-pointing to the owning Storage, annotated in the real source with
    "// TODO(@rtm0): Do not depend on Storage" — an acknowledged, unfixed layering inversion.
    indexDB additionally keeps a whole parallel legacy dual-index subsystem alive alongside the
    current per-partition index for backward-compatible migration, and Storage/table/partition
    each independently start and manage their own background merge/retention goroutines rather
    than sharing one lifecycle mechanism. Two of the package's per-item caches
    (metric_id_cache.go and date_metric_id_cache.go) are near-copy-paste of each other. None of
    this is idealized away in this cell's documentation — it reflects the real, messy shape of
    the code as of this pinned commit.

Annotations: |
  This cell is VictoriaMetrics's core time-series storage engine: it owns ingestion (AddRows),
  the inverted index (tag/label -> metric ID lookups), on-disk columnar block storage, and the
  streaming query iterator (`Search`) that app/vmselect's query path consumes. Every top-level
  app/* binary in this repository (vmstorage, vminsert, vmselect, the single-node
  victoria-metrics binary) depends on this cell directly or via app/vmstorage; it has no
  outbound dependency on any app/* package.

  Use `god_package` before extending this cell — changes here have the widest blast radius of
  any package in the repository.

  Use `Table` from Imports to understand how the inverted index is actually persisted: indexDB
  (an internal, unexported layer of this cell) is a domain-specific layer of tag-filter and
  per-day/global index logic built entirely on top of one `Table` instance from lib/mergeset,
  which knows nothing about tags or metric IDs.

---

"Storage(path: string, opts: OpenOptions)":
  location: storage.go
  annotations: |
    Top-level facade for one on-disk time-series database instance. Obtained via the
    MustOpenStorage factory. Internally owns exactly one table, which shards data into
    calendar-month partitions, each with its own inverted index — see `god_package` for the
    real (messier) internal shape this facade sits in front of.
  methods:
    "AddRows(mrs: []MetricRow, precisionBits: uint8)": |
      Ingest a batch of raw samples: resolve or assign each row's `TSID`, append to the active
      partition's raw-row buffer, and register new metric names in the index as needed. Panics
      (does not return an error) on unrecoverable failures, consistent with this method's real
      signature having no return value.

      `precisionBits`: controls lossy rounding of stored float values for compression
    "RegisterMetricNames(qt: QueryTracer, mrs: []MetricRow)": |
      Ensure every metric name in `mrs` exists in the index without ingesting any samples for
      it (used to pre-warm the index ahead of a future write). No return value.
    "SearchTSIDs(qt: QueryTracer, tfss: []TagFilters, tr: TimeRange, maxMetrics: int, deadline: uint64) -> tsids:[]TSID, err:error": |
      Resolve every `TagFilters` (OR'd, AND'd internally per filter) matching series within
      `tr` to their `TSID`s, capped at `maxMetrics`.
    "SearchMetricNames(qt: QueryTracer, tfss: []TagFilters, tr: TimeRange, maxMetrics: int, deadline: uint64) -> names:[]string, err:error": |
      Same matching as SearchTSIDs, returning marshaled `MetricName` strings instead.
    "SearchLabelNames(qt: QueryTracer, tfss: []TagFilters, tr: TimeRange, maxLabelNames: int, maxMetrics: int, deadline: uint64) -> names:[]string, err:error": |
      Enumerate distinct label names appearing on series matching `tfss` within `tr`, resolving
      at most `maxMetrics` series while scanning.
    "SearchLabelValues(qt: QueryTracer, labelName: string, tfss: []TagFilters, tr: TimeRange, maxLabelValues: int, maxMetrics: int, deadline: uint64) -> values:[]string, err:error": |
      Enumerate distinct values of `labelName` appearing on series matching `tfss` within `tr`,
      resolving at most `maxMetrics` series while scanning.
    "DeleteSeries(qt: QueryTracer, tfss: []TagFilters, maxMetrics: int) -> deleted:int, err:error": |
      Mark every series matching `tfss` as deleted (tombstoned in the index; underlying blocks
      are reclaimed on a later merge), returning the count removed.
    "GetSeriesCount(deadline: uint64) -> count:uint64, err:error": |
      Return the total number of distinct (non-deleted) series currently indexed.
    "GetTSDBStatus(qt: QueryTracer, tfss: []TagFilters, date: uint64, focusLabel: string, topN: int, maxMetrics: int, deadline: uint64) -> status:TSDBStatus, err:error": |
      Compute cardinality-diagnostic statistics (top label names/values by series count) for one
      day, optionally focused on one label.
    "MustCreateSnapshot() -> path:string": |
      Create a consistent, hard-linked point-in-time snapshot of the whole storage instance and
      return its path.
    "IsReadOnly() -> readOnly:bool": |
      Report whether the instance has switched itself to read-only (e.g. due to a free-disk-space
      limit being hit).
    "DebugFlush()": |
      Force all buffered in-memory data across every partition to become immediately searchable
      (tests/admin endpoints only).
    "UpdateMetrics(m: Metrics)": |
      Populate `m` with the storage instance's current size/throughput/cache counters.
    "MustClose()": |
      Stop all background goroutines across storage/table/partition/indexDB layers and release
      resources.

"OpenOptions(retention: time.Duration, futureRetention: time.Duration, maxHourlySeries: int, maxDailySeries: int, disablePerDayIndex: bool)":
  location: storage.go
  annotations: |
    Startup configuration passed to the `Storage` factory. Not mutable after open; changing
    retention or series-limit settings requires reopening the instance.

"MetricRow(metricNameRaw: []byte, timestamp: int64, value: float64)":
  location: storage.go
  annotations: |
    One raw ingested sample as it crosses from app/vminsert/app/vmagent into this cell.
  methods:
    "Marshal(dst: []byte) -> data:[]byte": |
      Append this row's binary encoding to `dst`.
    "UnmarshalX(src: []byte) -> tail:[]byte, err:error": |
      Decode one row from the front of `src`, returning the remaining unparsed bytes.
    "CopyFrom(src: MetricRow)": |
      Deep-copy another row's fields into this one (avoids an allocation on the hot ingestion
      path).

"MetricName(metricGroup: []byte, tags: []Tag)":
  location: metric_name.go
  annotations: |
    Canonical, sorted representation of a series' identity: its metric name plus all label
    (Tag) key/value pairs. Sync.Pool-backed (GetMetricName/PutMetricName) since it is
    constructed on every ingested row.
  methods:
    "AddTag(key: string, value: string)": |
      Append one label; tags must be (re-)sorted via the Marshal method before use as an index key.
    "RemoveTag(key: string)": |
      Remove the label named `key`, if present.
    "GetTagValue(key: string) -> value:[]byte": |
      Look up one label's value, or nil if absent.
    "Marshal(dst: []byte) -> data:[]byte": |
      Sort tags and append the canonical binary encoding to `dst` — this encoding is the actual
      index key used throughout the inverted index.
    "Unmarshal(src: []byte) -> err:error": |
      Decode a `MetricName` previously produced by its own Marshal method.

"TSID(metricGroupID: uint64, jobID: uint32, instanceID: uint32, metricID: uint64)":
  location: tsid.go
  annotations: |
    Fixed-width (24-byte), fully-ordered on-disk key identifying one series. Sorted first by
    `metricGroupID`, then `jobID`, then `instanceID`, then `metricID`, so that series sharing a
    metric name/job/instance sort contiguously — the layout blocks and searches are built around.
  methods:
    "Marshal(dst: []byte) -> data:[]byte": |
      Append the 24-byte binary encoding to `dst`.
    "Unmarshal(src: []byte) -> tail:[]byte": |
      Decode from the front of `src`, returning the remaining bytes.
    "Less(b: TSID) -> isLess:bool": |
      Total ordering comparison used throughout merge/search heap implementations.

"TagFilters()":
  location: tag_filters.go
  annotations: |
    Public, mutable builder for one AND-combined set of label matchers used as a query's filter.
    The actual regexp-optimization/matching logic (literal vs. regexp vs. negated matching,
    common-prefix extraction) lives in an unexported per-filter type with a process-global
    regexp cache — not part of this cell's public contract.
  methods:
    "Add(key: []byte, value: []byte, isNegative: bool, isRegexp: bool) -> err:error": |
      Append one matcher: key=value (or key!=value, key=~value, key!~value depending on
      `isNegative`/`isRegexp`).

"Search()":
  location: search.go
  annotations: |
    Public streaming query iterator over matching blocks, consumed by app/vmselect's
    query-execution path. Internally cascades through unexported per-tier iterators
    (table -> partition -> part), each merging its children's results via its own
    container/heap-based merge.
  properties:
    "MetricBlockRef -> MetricBlockRef": |
      The lazy block reference at the iterator's current position, valid after a successful
      call to the NextMetricBlock method.
  methods:
    "Init(qt: QueryTracer, storage: Storage, tfss: []TagFilters, tr: TimeRange, maxMetrics: int, deadline: uint64) -> matched:int": |
      Begin a new search: resolve matching `TSID`s for `tfss` within `tr`, capped at
      `maxMetrics`, returning the number matched.
    "NextMetricBlock() -> found:bool": |
      Advance to the next matching block; false once exhausted.
    "Error() -> err:error": |
      Report any error encountered during iteration.
    "MustClose()": |
      Release resources held by this search.

"Block(tsid: TSID, timestamps: []int64, values: []int64, scale: int16, precisionBits: uint8)":
  location: block.go
  annotations: |
    One decoded columnar chunk of (timestamp, value) pairs for a single series, as read from or
    about to be written to a part.
  methods:
    "Init(tsid: TSID, timestamps: []int64, values: []int64, scale: int16, precisionBits: uint8)": |
      Reset this Block to represent a fresh, not-yet-encoded chunk of raw samples.
    "MarshalData(timestampsBlockOffset: uint64, valuesBlockOffset: uint64) -> timestampsData:[]byte, valuesData:[]byte": |
      Compress and encode this block's timestamps/values columns for on-disk storage.
    "UnmarshalData() -> err:error": |
      Decompress and decode this block's stored columns back into timestamps/values.
    "AppendRowsWithTimeRangeFilter(dstTimestamps: []int64, dstValues: []float64, tr: TimeRange) -> timestamps:[]int64, values:[]float64": |
      Append only the rows within `tr` from this (already-decoded) block onto the destination
      slices.

"SearchQuery(start: int64, end: int64, tagFilterss: [][]TagFilter, maxMetrics: int)":
  location: search.go
  annotations: |
    Wire-format query DSL carried across the vminsert/vmselect RPC boundary describing a time
    range plus one or more OR'd, AND-combined TagFilter sets.
  methods:
    "Marshal(dst: []byte) -> data:[]byte": |
      Append this query's binary encoding to `dst`.
    "Unmarshal(src: []byte) -> err:error": |
      Decode a `SearchQuery` previously produced by its own Marshal method.

